From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamplay-mac <steamplay-mac@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Don't resolve imports of 32-bit steamclient.dll.

Valve's b1cce9c420 moved the 32-bit steamclient.dll handling into the
is_steamclient32 branch but changed `flags |= DONT_RESOLVE_DLL_REFERENCES`
to `flags |= LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS`. build_module() tests `flags` against
DONT_RESOLVE_DLL_REFERENCES (0x1), not LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS (0x40000000),
so the imports of the 32-bit steamclient.dll were resolved again. Its
imports tier0_s.dll and vstdlib_s.dll are not present (only the 64-bit
ones are, and those are redirected to ntdll), so fixup_imports() fails,
the module never loads and 32-bit games fail SteamAPI_Init().

Restore the pre-b1cce9c420 32-bit behaviour (c177a34d78/0ec337a475):
skip import resolution; LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS stays set in the modref, so
process_attach()/MODULE_InitDLL() skip it as before. The 64-bit
steamclient64/gameoverlayrenderer path (LDR_DONT_CALL_DLLMAIN) is
unchanged.
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index c4acbb0..f61c938 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -2366,8 +2366,12 @@ static NTSTATUS build_module( LPCWSTR load_path, const UNICODE_STRING *nt_name,
             DWORD protect_old;
             HANDLE file;
 
+            /* 32-bit steamclient.dll is fully replaced by lsteamclient trampolines; its
+             * imports (tier0_s.dll, vstdlib_s.dll) must not be resolved and DllMain must
+             * not run. LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS is a WINE_MODREF flag, the fixup below tests
+             * the LoadLibraryEx flag DONT_RESOLVE_DLL_REFERENCES. */
             wm->ldr.Flags |= LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS;
-            flags |= LDR_DONT_RESOLVE_REFS;
+            flags |= DONT_RESOLVE_DLL_REFERENCES;
 
             NtProtectVirtualMemory( NtCurrentProcess(), &addr, &size, PAGE_READWRITE, &protect_old );
             memset( &attr, 0, sizeof(attr) );
-- 
